## Billing Rules

- **Trial length:** Always read from `get_current_rate('owner_trial_days')` via `platform_pricing` table
- **Never hardcode 90** (or any trial duration) anywhere in application code
- **Prices:** Always read from `platform_pricing` — never hardcoded in UI or API
- **Feature flags:** Always read `stripe_checkout_enabled` from `feature_flags` table at runtime — not from env vars or hardcoded booleans
- **Owner billing before PM billing** — PM Growth/Professional/Enterprise tiers are Phase 2
- **Subscription access rule:** `status IN ('trialing', 'active')` = allow. All other statuses = prompt to subscribe.
- **Webhook idempotency:** Use Stripe event ID to deduplicate. Stripe can deliver the same event more than once.
- **Billing page gate:** Read `feature_flags` directly (not via `has_feature_access`) — `has_feature_access` requires an existing subscription; the billing page runs before one exists
- **Annual price key:** `owner_essentials_annual` — read via `get_current_rate('owner_essentials_annual')`
- **Monthly price key:** `owner_essentials_monthly` — read via `get_current_rate('owner_essentials_monthly')`
- **STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET:** `.env.local` currently holds the Stripe CLI local secret — swap for the dashboard webhook secret before any production deployment
