## Scope Guards — What NOT to Build

Unless there is an explicit decision in the spec, do not build:

- **Statement revenue view** — cash basis attribution to checkout month. Phase 2. Separate feature.
- **vs. Fcst tab** — forecast variance. Phase 2. `pm_forecasts` table exists but tab is not active.
- **Waterfall tab** — revenue bridge. Phase 2.
- **Pacing view** — future bookings vs. forecast. Phase 2.
- **PM billing tiers** (Growth / Professional / Enterprise) — Phase 2. Owner billing ships first.
- **CYTD forecast comparison** — Phase 2. Period structure is in place; only the comparison series changes.
- **RevPAR Index normalization / bedroom cohort** — Phase 2 refinement.
- **Quarter toggle** — removed in v1.4. Do not re-add.
- **All Time toggle** — removed in v1.4. Do not re-add.
- **RevPAR denominator** — always `available_nights`. ADR denominator — always `prorated_booked_nights` (`guestBookedNights`). These must never be swapped.
- **Cross-property contamination** — `computePeriodStats` groups bookings by `property_id` before computing available nights. Never apply one property's owner/maintenance blocks to another property's denominator.
- **Index card** — deferred to Sprint 17. Final card order: Revenue | RevPAR | Occ% | ADR | Index.
- **favicon.ico location:** Must be in `app/favicon.ico` — Next.js serves `app/` before `public/`. Replacing only `public/favicon.ico` has no effect.
- **computePeriodStats is async:** Always await it. Call sites must use useEffect + state, not useMemo.
- **market_benchmarks:** No `week_start_date` column. Always derive ISO week Monday via `to_date(year::text || '-' || week_number::text, 'IYYY-IW')`.
